==Taxonomy==
It was described in 1856 by [[George Engelmann]] as ''Mammillaria micromeris'' var. ''greggii'', and was later elevated to species status and transferred to the genus ''Epithelantha'' by Charles Russell Orcutt in 1926. The species name greggii honors the American naturalist [[Josiah Gregg]].<ref name="l204">{{cite web | title=Epithelantha greggii | website=International Plant Names Index | url=https://www.ipni.org/n/92860-2 | access-date=2026-07-28}}</ref>
